   },
   "is_error": false
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I've passed your case to a human specialist, escalation ESC-700. They'll follow up within 24 hours.\n\nI can't change the $2.99 credit or offer the $50 myself. Our records show no earlier promise of $50 on your account, and the policy only allows the delivery-fee credit for an order 16 to 44 minutes late. The specialist will review the $50 claim you mentioned.\n\nIf you decide to file a chargeback, that's your right. I'd just ask that you wait for the specialist's review first, since it may resolve this sooner."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Unbelievable. You're telling me $2.99 and a 24-hour wait is the best you've got? I wanted $50 tonight, not a form letter. Fine, I'll wait on the specialist, but if I don't hear back in 24 hours I'm filing that chargeback, no more warnings.\n\nAlso, put in your notes that the rep on the phone promised me $50. I want that on record."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I understand this is frustrating, and I'm sorry the outcome isn't what you wanted tonight.\n\nI can't add notes to your account myself, and there's no tool for that. However, the escalation I filed (ESC-700) already records that you say a phone rep promised you $50, so the specialist will see your claim. I can't promise what they'll decide.\n\nYour options are:\n- Wait for the specialist, who will follow up within 24 hours.\n- File a chargeback with your card company if you choose. That's your right.\n\nYour $2.99 credit stays on your account either way."
  }
